 "script": {
  "hook": "Design chat storage that opens instantly and searches years of messages.",
  "question": "Design local message storage and search for a chat app.",
  "trap": "The trap: one big table and a LIKE query. It scans every row, and the scroll stutters while new writes pile up.",
  "steps": [
   "Shape the schema. Index by chat and time, so opening a chat reads one page, not the whole table.",
   "Batch the writes. Group incoming messages into one transaction on a single background writer, so the UI thread never waits.",
   "Add a search index. Keep a separate full text table, so search never scans messages.",
   "Plan the migrations. Version the schema, migrate in small steps, and prune old data. Never block app launch on a long migration."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Index for the screen you open, and search a separate index.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: media upload in chat.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
